            <ArticleTitle>Intracoronary thrombectomy: a new approach to total occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>244-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>After initial failure with conventional angioplasty of a total right coronary artery occlusion, we were successful in obtaining patency using a combination of intracoronary thrombectomy and thrombolysis. This represents the first report of this technique in the therapy of total right coronary occlusions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
